// A CJK lyric (kana / ideograph / Hangul) fills the em square, so its ink reaches
// higher than any Latin word. The lyric line must drop far enough to clear notes that
// dip below the staff — otherwise the tall glyphs overlap the low noteheads. The low
// c/d run here (below the treble staff) locks that clearance.
title "CJK lyric clears low notes"
time 4/4
key c major
part m { clef treble section A { c4 c d e | } }
lyrics words { section A { き ら き ら | } }
form main { A }
score main "cjk-lyric-clears-notes" { staff m with lyrics words }
